And as a performance enhancement specialist,

00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,940
the corrective exercise specialist,

00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:11,300
training and being a nutritionist working

00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:15,180
with individuals was my day-to-day operation

00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:17,780
and experimentation, not only at that point

00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:21,580
with my own physiology but with many, many other people.

00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:25,180
And then I actually went to medical school for a couple years,

00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:28,740
hated it, went to a PhD program in clinical psychology,

00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:30,500
completed all three years of coursework,

00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:34,900
and then really decided I want to move back to my roots

00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:40,380
in nutrition and exercise and lifestyle choices to be healthy.

00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:42,380
And I've also done a master's in human nutrition

00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,580
and functional medicine.

00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,460
I think this base of experimentation

00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:48,260
with human physiology is really important.

00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:53,180
And I would also add, there's a really interesting distinction

00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:57,140
between a focus on pathology and disease

00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:59,300
versus a focus on health.

00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:04,300
And the whole conventional medical paradigm, certainly,

00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:07,740
is really a disease paradigm.

00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:09,340
It's a pathology paradigm.

00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:12,100
It's the study of disease.

00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,780
And the whole paradigm is sort of based

00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:17,900
on a conceptual framework that says,

00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:21,780
if we study the biochemical mechanisms of disease,

00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:25,220
we can figure out, quote unquote, the cause of the disease,

00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,980
for example, depression is caused by a,

00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:32,180
caused quote unquote by a deficiency in serotonin in the brain

00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:37,460
or atherosclerosis and heart disease is caused by LDL cholesterol

00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:39,620
and so on and so forth.

00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:44,100
And then based on that understanding of pathology,

00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:48,540
it seeks to create drugs that interrupt what it perceives

00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:51,140
to be abnormal physiology, to interrupt

00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:53,460
those disease processes.

00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:58,460
And then by virtue of interrupting abnormal biochemical

00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:02,420
mechanisms that are associated with disease,

00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:05,220
the idea is that would reverse the disease

00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:08,900
or cure the disease or at least hopefully correct

00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:11,140
some of the symptoms of it.

00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:14,260
And there's a context where that model works really well

00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:18,860
in battlefield medicine and wartime medicine

00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,940
and even in the context of emergency medicine

00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:25,180
and dealing with acute infections.

00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:28,340
It can be antibiotics, can be life saving.

00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:29,940
But when it comes to chronic disease,

00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:33,540
the model has really been a massive failure.

00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:38,540
And what I think is that it's been a failure largely

00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:42,220
because of the focus on disease.

00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:45,900
I think studying disease is not a great way

00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,900
to learn how to be healthy.

00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:50,300
It's different sets of tools.

00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:53,820
And if we want to be healthy and prevent disease

00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:56,780
and I would argue in most cases the best treatment

00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:59,740
for most diseases was some exceptions,

00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:03,100
the best treatment is actually to create health.

00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:07,660
And so the whole paradigm needs to be upended.

00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:10,380
If we actually want to create health,

00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:13,420
we need to stop fixating on the study of disease

00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:16,740
and start studying the science of creating health.

00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:19,060
We're looking at it completely backwards

00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,340
what you're saying.

00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:21,340
Yeah.

00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:26,940
So how do you, you get an average person

00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:30,020
that maybe has some sort of autoimmune disease

00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:31,500
or something like that?

00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:35,260
How do you get them from that medical model

00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:40,100
into a more functional health lifestyle model

00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:45,100
that it's an educational process, isn't it?

00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:46,180
It is.

00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:48,500
Yeah. And here's a big shift in thinking.

00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:49,540
This is really interesting.

00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:53,180
I find a lot of people don't know this.

00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,380
I've been shocked actually also

00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:56,140
at the amount of practitioners that don't know this.

00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,660
But it's really important.

00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:02,980
You're kind of extending out from what I was just talking about.

00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:06,220
There's a lot of research to show that even if we,

00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,660
well actually let me step back for a second.

00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:12,180
So the whole central core Western medical paradigm is

00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:13,820
we need to, there's this disease

00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:15,500
and there's that disease, heart disease

00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,100
and cancer, neurological disease

00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,500
and obesity and diabetes.

00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:22,220
And if only we could find cures for these diseases.

00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:24,340
And the assumption built into this

00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,220
is that if we had a cure for heart disease,

00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:30,220
if we had a cure for cancer, et cetera,

00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:33,100
that we would just live so much longer.

00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:36,100
And in fact, this paradigm is completely not true.

00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,380
This assumption is totally wrong.

00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:41,300
It's actually been shown in numerous studies

00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:44,660
that if we had a cure for heart disease tomorrow,

00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:48,020
heart disease is the number one killer in the Western world.

00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:49,500
If we had a cure for it tomorrow,

00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:53,820
it would actually barely budge the average lifespan.

00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:55,700
The same is true for cancer, the same is true

00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,420
for all the other major diseases

00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,820
that we are desperately in search of a cure for.

00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:04,060
And the reason why is that these are largely diseases

00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:07,260
of lifestyle and environment that are,

00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:10,700
it's not just one part of the body

00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:12,300
that has some kind of dysfunction.

00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:17,180
It's widespread dysfunctional physiology

00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:19,180
and poor metabolic health,

00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:24,180
that's creating dysfunction in numerous systems of the body.

00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:26,980
And then basically the diagnosis of what disease you get

00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:30,380
is essentially whatever disease process happens

00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:33,700
to emerge first, sort of based on your weakest link.

00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:36,300
But it's not like if you remove that piece,

00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,100
the rest of you is completely healthy

00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:40,660
and is gonna live a much longer period of time.

00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:45,300
In fact, the research shows that basically

00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:48,220
if somebody didn't die of heart disease at age 79,

00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:50,300
they'd probably die of cancer at age 80.

00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:52,740
And if they didn't die of cancer at age 80,

00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:55,740
they'd die of complications from diabetes

00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:59,700
or neurological disease at age 80 and a half or 81.

00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:02,900
And if all of those diseases are cured,

00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:05,900
it would still barely budge the average lifespan

00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:09,500
because most people's whole body essentially breaks down.

00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:14,500
You get multi organ failure on average by about age 85.

00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:18,340
In other words, people die of quote unquote old age.

00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:21,420
That's what dying of old ages is basically the body

00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:24,540
as a whole becomes so broken and dysfunctional

00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:26,740
that you get multi organ system failure.

00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:29,540
Your body just says no more and it taps out.

00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:31,060
And here's the key point.

00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:34,380
The actual maximal genetic human lifespan

00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:38,540
isn't age 85, it's around 120.

00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:43,540
So the real key, if we want to really live longer,

00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:47,140
it's not to cure this disease and to cure that disease

00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,220
and to cure this disease.

00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:50,380
It's actually to learn the science around

00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:54,420
how do we slow the rate of aging as much as possible

00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:58,100
at the cellular level so that we are on average

00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:01,180
reaching close to 120 of the maximal

00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,020
genetically determined human lifespan

00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:06,540
as opposed to dying 30 or 40 years sooner

00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:10,020
from basically accelerated cellular aging

00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:12,340
and dysfunctional metabolic health.

00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:15,060
Yeah, so the named disease that the person

00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:17,980
may be currently suffering from is just the effect

00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:22,220
of the epigenetic choices that that person has made

00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:27,220
that is basically breaking down metabolic pathways.

00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:28,660
Right.

00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:32,540
It's like if you see somebody, you do a blood test

00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:37,060
